## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

This is a textbook **"coverage-farming"** test suite. Every production method is called (→ 95% line coverage), but almost nothing meaningful is asserted. Here's the severity-ranked breakdown:

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — Assert-Free Tests (coverage with zero verification)

These tests execute code but never check outcomes. Any regression will pass silently.

**1. `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)** — No assert at all. Never verifies the product was actually stored.

```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var saved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", saved!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, saved.Price);
```

**2. `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32)** — Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the price changed.

```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

**3. `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38)** — Calls `RemoveProduct` but never checks it's gone.

```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

**4. `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)** — No assert. Also tests against an empty catalog, so even adding an assert on `count` being `0` would be trivial.

```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-002", "Gadget", 19.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(2, _catalog.GetProductCount());
```

**5. `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)** — Applies a 10% discount but never checks that prices changed. A no-op implementation would pass.

```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
var w = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
var g = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002");
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, w!.Price);   // 9.99 * 0.90
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, g!.Price);  // 19.99 * 0.90
```

**6. `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 84)** — Imports CSV but never verifies a product was created.

```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var product = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(product);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", product!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, product.Price);
```

